WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.967
Hello everyone. My name is Zhicheng Wang.

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:05.600
In this video, I will explore how robotics

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.000
can contribute to the Sustainable Development Goals.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.100
Industrial robots automate production.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.000
Service robots perform useful tasks for people or equipment.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.100
Industrial robots weld and assemble products.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.133
Consumer robots clean homes and support learning.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:34.333
Professional robots transport goods, clean workplaces and cultivate crops.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:40.000
Medical robots assist surgery, diagnosis and rehabilitation.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.800
A robot measures its surroundings using sensors.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.000
A controller chooses a command, and actuators produce movement.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.867
Feedback repeats this cycle.

00:00:52.867 --> 00:01:00.000
When conditions change, new measurements update the command and the robot adjusts.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.200
The United Nations' seventeen Sustainable Development Goals

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:10.000
guide action for people and planet.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.267
Autonomous boats map water quality.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:20.000
Their measurements can guide further investigation.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.100
Educational robots let learners test sensing and control.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:30.000
These experiments can build technical skills.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.733
Robotic disassembly separates components for recovery.

00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:40.000
Recovery also depends on damage and energy use.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.833
Agricultural robots can locate weeds and target treatment.

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:50.000
Results depend on conditions in the field.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.300
Rehabilitation robots assist movement under clinical supervision.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:00.000
Patient consent remains essential.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.267
Underwater robots photograph the seabed.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:10.000
Located images help researchers assess marine habitats.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.500
Blade crawlers record wind turbine surfaces.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:20.000
Engineers use inspection records to plan maintenance.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.267
Remote-controlled machines separate operators from demolition.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:30.000
Training and controlled work zones remain essential.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.400
Robotic printers place concrete layer by layer.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:40.000
Assess materials, energy and service life.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.267
We now examine sustainable agriculture.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:50.000
Can robots remove weeds without harming crops?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.233
Crops and weeds compete for water, light and nutrients.

00:02:55.233 --> 00:03:00.000
Control weeds while protecting crops.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.667
Define the field boundary and plan the planting lines.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:10.000
The robot aligns with this plan.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.267
Each seed is placed and its position recorded.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:20.000
The robot uses this map on later visits.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.267
Positioning connects the machine to its seed map.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:30.000
Commands depend on tool position and timing.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.267
The tool loosens soil between the crop lines.

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:40.000
The loosened plants remain on the surface.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.267
Small knives enter gaps between neighbouring plants.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:50.000
They retract near stored crop positions.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.267
Mechanical weeding may reduce herbicide use.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:04:00.000
Inspect the field and plan further control.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.267
Sunlight and workload affect battery endurance.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:10.000
Soil, weather and weed size affect performance.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.267
Compare remaining weeds and crop injury.

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:20.000
Count all labour, energy and follow-up work.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.633
Position errors can direct tools towards crops.

00:04:24.633 --> 00:04:30.000
Keep human override and define responsibilities.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.933
Robots change work and can put incomes at risk.

00:04:34.933 --> 00:04:40.000
Fund training and involve affected workers.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.267
Shared services may widen access.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:50.000
Agree repair support and control of farm records.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.233
I am Zhicheng Wang.

00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:53.200
Thank you for watching my video.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.600
If you are interested in robotics too,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.000
I'd love to hear from you.
